d/id #uuid "9724f003-06ea-5591-8da2-04eeaa531ee3" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d26247f5-ea0b-58f7-ab8c-9e2873f56e29" :question/math-academy-id "q-170844" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n- **P.** $P:{1,2,3}\\cap {4,5,6}=∅$\n- **Q.** $Q:\\sqrt{{3}^{2}-{4}^{2}}$\n- **R.** $R:4$ is a prime number.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because the intersection of the given sets is empty.\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *false* since $4$ is not prime.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88ca2b5c-6791-591f-abda-f27884967edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459617} {:answer/id #uuid "c56bf6b0-66f4-518a-a6ce-ba874d1a9c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c56bf6b0-66f4-518a-a6ce-ba874d1a9c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459618} :answer-field/id #uuid "24a6ed8a-17b7-51a7-bb49-dcf74e7ade9b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04cb5f8b-73b3-5617-abfc-6b43148614ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459619} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8f35e0-edab-543a-a110-589cb05bd8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f8f35e0-edab-543a-a110-589cb05bd8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459620} :answer-field/id #uuid "96184caa-a44f-51b9-bafe-5eddcc9cb49b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acb09f9b-41e0-580c-a041-095bbce4770b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459621} {:answer/id #uuid "868a0a7e-8c6e-5345-b4ea-51218d4e274a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acb09f9b-41e0-580c-a041-095bbce4770b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459621} :answer-field/id #uuid "42968c23-3a57-5e5b-b613-c57e6362a57d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5327827-bdd3-59f2-8ac3-6f2fcb1af21e" :question/math-academy-id "q-171486" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n- **I.** $P(n):$ $n$ is even.\n- **II.** $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}-x\\ge 1$\n- **III.** $R(y):$ Draw a line of width $y\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give an instruction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f1de0a5-72af-5067-ac6a-f1db1793d9bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459665} {:answer/id #uuid "4042b04c-c83e-506d-aaee-db575f15ae1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f1de0a5-72af-5067-ac6a-f1db1793d9bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459665} :answer-field/id #uuid "7edf7cbb-6689-5715-877d-fe1220e7c9c8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc25a2ca-8725-573a-8fb6-a0f677d677a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459667} {:answer/id #uuid "80e2bd40-7cd5-5b6d-ae6c-0db9109c48e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80e2bd40-7cd5-5b6d-ae6c-0db9109c48e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459668} :answer-field/id #uuid "84bf1ea9-21f9-5b78-83e6-32eeb73acd61" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a11266d-86a1-5fe9-ab8b-9e576674a081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459669} {:answer/id #uuid "2b9c94fc-bb95-591e-8055-4c0c344d9261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a11266d-86a1-5fe9-ab8b-9e576674a081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459669} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eac2805-d927-5131-a557-7a329c3675c8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59457bab-d41c-5c4d-af91-59c9dc67dad9" :question/math-academy-id "q-181294" :question/problem "If $A=\\{0,1,2\\}$ and $B=\\{x,y\\},$ which of the following elements belong to $(A\\times B)\\times A?$\n\nI. $(1,y,2)$\n\nII. $((1,y),2)$\n\nIII. $((y,1),y)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${0,1,2}$ with ${x,y},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/07/077da578323a686ecf0e07cf0a56030fa4ce128a74d408af95b8a3027ad13f28.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(0,x),(0,y),(1,x),(1,y),(2,x),(2,y)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=3\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(A\\times B)\\times A\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A\\times B$ and $A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/3a/3a14abffc755dcfccce2d410ea18fbcae42d4afe2fbeffd81e1a291bc9d4968e.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(A\\times B)\\times A|=|A\\times B|\\cdot |A|=6\\cdot 3=18.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $((1,y),2)\\in (A\\times B)\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62c177a9-2328-5eaf-88c0-9a311b033aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459671} {:answer/id #uuid "1b79aa1f-fa03-518a-a250-98c638dfe2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b79aa1f-fa03-518a-a250-98c638dfe2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459672} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1493459-b197-58a9-b9fb-9a679fa44