lue "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3415ccd-bcd7-576e-9e22-7076b1cb7814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460274} :answer-field/id #uuid "37c4a1b2-25b2-522d-9152-8a556721c75d" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2a941ac-46f5-56a9-b5ba-03889446453a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80336" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${R}_{0}^{-}?$\n- **I.** $-\\pi $\n- **II.** $\\sqrt{3}$\n- **III.** $-\\frac{4}{5}$\n- **IV.** $0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${R}_{0}^{-}$ is the set of all negative real numbers and $0.$\n\n- $-\\pi $ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $\\sqrt{3}$ is a positive number, so it does *not* belong to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\frac{4}{5}$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $0$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d56b033-a2c8-57c7-adde-e574d726ec78" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting Symbolic Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b2bb64d-c43d-5ec6-934e-e53eedd3cbdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459705} {:answer/id #uuid "07fdfcee-63eb-5dc7-a357-64cb51c29abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07fdfcee-63eb-5dc7-a357-64cb51c29abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459706} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9f911be-0b6c-5c4f-89de-532889e92395" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "872a53b7-39d7-542b-83fc-7a7d9f2d3d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459707} {:answer/id #uuid "586967bd-21bb-5beb-9fc4-854b7d8831c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "586967bd-21bb-5beb-9fc4-854b7d8831c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459708} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef6c49d-d45b-5a59-a2ea-1ea63ddfe9c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460720} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37ba7205-2106-5ef0-9ed6-ab1f3f726736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459709} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa92fc9-03e6-57dc-9911-40ad3d1d7c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37ba7205-2106-5ef0-9ed6-ab1f3f726736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459709} :answer-field/id #uuid "222d5208-0c8d-53a7-9d1a-051fc3b939a2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "866aa1bc-982d-58ab-8e07-dd5148fa5235" :question/math-academy-id "q-182470" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $P⇒Q≡¬P∨Q$\n- **II.** $¬(P⇒Q)≡P∧¬Q$\n- **III.** $¬(P⇒Q)≡P∨¬Q$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬P∨Q.$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. From part I, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\nP⇒Q≡¬P∨Q\n$$\n\nBy negating this statement, we get\n\n$$\n¬(P⇒Q)≡¬(¬P∨Q).\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n¬(¬P∨Q)≡¬(¬P)∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nP∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nSo, $¬(P⇒Q)$ is equivalent to $P∧¬Q.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d65819f-0528-527e-8d1a-20421e221ca5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Coterminal Angles in Radians"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d12f60a-1b4b-5ad9-8170-fad04c575573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459743} {:answer/id #uuid "97f66db8-2896-5bf4-9c6a-c7155f7aac88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97f66db8-2896-5bf4-9c6a-c7155f7aac88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459744} :answer-field/id #uuid "964ed19f-e4e4-56df-85c8-9a070f5bba74" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2047179-53d8-50a5-845b-dfed41f6bdb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459745} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7b3e3f-7bd9-5a09-b737-93ecdd282f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd7b3e3f-7bd9-5a09-b737-93ecdd282f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459746} :answer-field/id #uuid "7aca4bf5-1448-51b9-959a-aea79faa2142" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7a74c92-738c-5c1d-b1e6-ec2b894aaa51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459747} {:answer/id #uuid "26827bfb-0b07-5aca-b80e-e8fa2dbc4d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26827bfb-0b07-5aca-b80e-e8fa2dbc4d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459748} :answer-field/id #uuid "073e06f8-9a08-555f-888d-a160ccd25418" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7636651-ac27-54dd-bac3-a58cbd0f8a37" :question/math-academy-id "q-23191" :question/problem "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}?$\n- **I.** $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$\n- **II.** $\\frac{10\\pi }{3}$\n- **III.** $-\\frac{8\\pi }{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$:\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\cdot (2\\pi )=\\frac{10\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $\\frac{10\\pi }{3}.$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$:\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-2\\pi =-\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-\\frac{14\\pi }{3}$\n\nOf the given angles, all three are coterminal with $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I, II, and III."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064312 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd5c660-b216-59b4-b2bb-df83ef864b2a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Concave Up and Concave Down Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b93bee7b-9d95-5423-8e1c-399dda55a57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459547} {:answer/id #uuid "3e56b729-6fa4-570f-8237-64e14a77c120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b93bee7b-9d95-5423-8e1c-399dda55a57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459547} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb55ba0f-4c1f-545f-a843-c5924a912ae6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460640} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e608ff10-c867-526c-8a3d-571af0743728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459549