ion/id #uuid "183472b0-16c2-5809-99fd-33beade724a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-48344" :question/problem "![](images/09/09d006953b4fc1d111a84e78fcc6b2038d53768fb82d6f61a0b2a1d0126bbb40.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,0]$\n- $x\\in [-3,2]$\n- $x\\in (0,\\infty )$\n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,0]$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=-3.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $[-3,2].$ It is continuous on $(-3,2),$ and also right continuous at $x=-3$ and left continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(0,\\infty )$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078487 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f00fd821-a5d4-5844-9db5-795b9e321b94" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Largest Intervals of Continuity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1abb4819-32aa-5825-8aba-4fd7804637a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460059} {:answer/id #uuid "f35e1f11-2422-51e5-af6e-1235b12fd7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1abb4819-32aa-5825-8aba-4fd7804637a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460059} :answer-field/id #uuid "43e016e3-9a6a-572e-859b-c5130dd62a24" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident 