85 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd611935-717e-54db-b36b-c834b2cac00c" :question/math-academy-id "q-96858" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,1)$, $(2,1)$ and $(1,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(-2,1)$\n- **II.** $(-8,4)$\n- **III.** $(3,6)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-8,4)$, $(-12,6)$ and $(-2,1).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110587 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b834b64-9679-56c2-b5e9-ee26a54b5e13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values in the Domain of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "078d2924-166d-5429-aff7-90844485e0da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459969} {:answer/id #uuid "2eedd628-272b-5b7a-914d-ed8ff226c33b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2eedd628-272b-5b7a-914d-ed8ff226c33b" :answ