" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05f6d575-2f42-5773-86ea-0000d3bcfcd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-29095" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n- **I.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=10$\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$\n- **III.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation II has no solutions."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b2036f-da0f-59de-8a39-6b33e6cbdd04" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a True Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a433b800-1989-563e-83e7-5397c5645766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459769} {:answer/id #uuid "f27cd420-457b-52b0-be46-420933044538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f27cd420-457b-52b0-be46-420933044538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459770} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cb2e9f1-fb8f-51c5-b00d-72cffd6f3c70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87a1cebe-01c8-5058-9714-b637af1f37da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459771} {:answer/id #uuid "b3681972-1d5a-565f-8458-5b8fb369970e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87a1cebe-01c8-5058-9714-b637af1f37da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459771} :answer-field/id #uuid "66227881-d1e0-51a9-ab58-2ae984608738" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aeb3e0e-1388-5c9a-acdc-1e8fd08c915c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459773} {:answer/id #uuid "b0269478-23f2-5548-a846-c1bfeff061d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0269478-23f2-5548-a846-c1bfeff061d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459774} :answer-field/id #uuid "41ad434b-4089-5c1e-9be7-18886b5005e0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e42babae-3f60-5ad6-9c62-eaf91af5f106" :question/math-academy-id "q-32167" :question/problem "Which of the following completes the statement so that it is true:\n\n*If a $2\\times 2$-matrix $A$ is invertible, then $\\text{__________}$ . *\n- **I.** $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution\n- **II.** $Ax=0$ has infinitely many solutions\n- **III.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\nNow, since the first part of the invertible matrix theorem is true ($A$ is invertible), all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem, only options I and III give us true statements:\n\n- *If $A$ is invertible, then $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution.* $\\,✓$\n\n- *If $A$ is invertible, then $det(A)\\ne 0.$* $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Concerning a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b39e27f-13ee-501b-ba4b-5d78eda71cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459859} {:answer/id #uuid "42bc3d2f-47ac-5240-bebc-29d8ead2b2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42bc3d2f-47ac-5240-bebc-29d8ead2b2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459860} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd4b48c7-8b33-5b11-b0ff-fd23af78c621" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a88c44bd-6f41-5235-ac58-7911bde2559b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459861} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f3a730-a463-502e-ba29-0ea5209e14d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3f3a730-a463-502e-ba29-0ea5209e14d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459862} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e08014-03f2-546f-8c0e-728bfa9c9445" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6abd007-c716-5d06-8cfa-120ea1d604b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459863} {:answer/id #uuid "27573a68-3ee6-50f3-b43d-78e4538fb66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6abd007-c716-5d06-8cfa-120ea1d604b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459863} :answer-field/id #uuid "27edb236-0299-5bf2-b9d8-b04543e794ed" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f74e266c-1efa-53d7-993c-e40799d4cc74" :question/math-academy-id "q-36073" :question/problem "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $Ax=b$ in the usual way. Given that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $A$ is invertible\n- **II.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $Ax=0$ has an infinite number of solutions\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17aa9c3c-1177-5ab6-9436-4ed101b94dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459963} {:answer/id #uuid "37e030ed-add9-5c5c-b9c2-a9b03bda4a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17aa9c3c-1177-5ab6-9436-4ed101b94dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459963} :answer-field/id #uuid "575277b5-4a90-527e-97ae-d9ef4882fdfa" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3757cf46-44d8-5925-81e3-501b153e88c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459965} {:answer/id #uuid "9e164199-e408-5a69-9bc2-cd5d71bdf400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3757cf46-44d8-5925-81e3-501b153e88c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459965} :answer-field/id #uuid "053227d5-2248-514c-83ab-a486205fe2d4" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "921e04de-799e-5beb-ab08-d9814cdcfb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459967} {:answer/id #uuid "7574341a-6c1f-5a8e-961a-b129941c9412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7574341a-6c1f-5a8e-961a-b129941c9412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459968} :answer-field/id #uuid "9efeee9c-63b6-5691-bb36-c331fd5f912d" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12fdac9a-07ca-546f-8c67-8327e7b0318b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42134" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block diagonal?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block diagonal matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and all the other blocks contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block diagonal matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block diagonal matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a081c073-7785-5822-a590-7bfe5b3a0d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459993} {:answer/id #uuid "b0a6c82a-ea16-5ff3-8bdf-84c0339a862e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0a6c82a-ea16-5ff3-8bdf-84c0339a862e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459994} :answer-field/id #uuid "4819ddf4-8130-5b59-a61d-9183708e79f6" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c9400fe-5e9b-5eeb-8918-63a684f4e2ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459995} {:answer/id #uuid "000331dd-d687-50e7-840d-4298a5368dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9400fe-5e9b-5eeb-8918-63a684f4e2ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459995} :answer-field/id #uuid "234e20cd-9790-5bf2-8ab0-5d985b7db758" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460864} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a258fde-3dcf-564c-9b6b-f6a8c2ff2d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459997} {:answer/id #uuid "708f2b4d-d226-5732-a090-fd16b632ea2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a258fde-3dcf-564c-9b6b-f6a8c2ff2d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459997} :answer-field/id #uuid "12022d23-fdca-5fdc-a369-46e825b1e2e8" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60c27a10-b6b0-5a54-9d51-0c91bf9fbc6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42591" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $P$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrices $Q$ and $S$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ is an elementary matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d1574dd-091a-52ae-8eb0-535fd3914634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460005} {:answer/id #uuid "7586863f-229d-578d-ac84-f0e761139eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d1574dd-091a-52ae-8eb0-535fd3914634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460005} :answer-field/id #uuid "bec46523-5df6-5a30-a264-03c885caa2bd" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed431171-2bbf-5c8c-afad-a46ecfc1b548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460007} {:answer/id #uuid "8cfdbbbb-5343-5c70-85ff-8ea0242e36fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cfdbbbb-5343-5c70-85ff-8ea0242e36fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460008} :answer-field/id #uuid "e90e3cb2-cf8d-5f7e-8a1d-7e3fced79e84" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "849f41f5-f501-53ee-8ecc-b0fca7647ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460009} {:answer/id #uuid "b44c80de-5afb-5ae0-9c0e-9042718b52cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849f41f5-f501-53ee-8ecc-b0fca7647ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460009} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b060f26-347b-584a-9045-d8d27b9e7501" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90c835e0-83aa-519b-9995-715569dd5d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-43000" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80449399-3ae4-593f-8c3b-00bcdcc99727" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Trigonometric Equations Outside of the Range of Cosecant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45ba7a28-f5ab-5e8c-bc17-9d5aab25046f" :answer/type {:db/id #ed