nt :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f4e1182-d195-5cca-bb1a-601ea1f9c921" :question/math-academy-id "q-47599" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $det(A)=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}$\n- **III.** $A$ has $5$ pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=7=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=7,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $7$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129287 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Recurrence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "626de4c7-07ee-5308-9a23-934777925783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459757} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec59719-d576-5c4b-9f37-7da5426c5edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "626de4c7-07ee-5308-9a23-934777925783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459757} :answer-field/id #uuid "48acc387-a54c-50dd-aad6-585cf72b6a89" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59438dcb-5098-5a37-8a8a-0559a266526d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459759} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ea72a8-0138-57f7-8d42-142ef14c07ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59438dcb-5098-5a37-8a8a-0559a266526d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459759} :answer-field/id #uuid "340a7483-0648-538f-9e0e-c1dca3ac2efa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d03f0076-7577-5d1b-bc3c-65d3e9f63200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459761} {:answer/id #uuid "9b564c41-c975-557e-aaba-25711bc033d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b564c41-c975-557e-aaba-25711bc033d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459762} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d8ad94a-27a7-5b22-9374-cccd6a4e4e54" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13864329-1fa0-567c-b5b4-57dd540d6c9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-253143" :question/problem "Which of the following recurrence relations are first-order?\n- **I.** ${a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-2}$\n- **II.** ${b}_{n}={b}_{n-1}^{2}+2{b}_{n-2}$\n- **III.** ${c}_{n}=2{c}_{n-1}+n$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${c}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129321 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "359bc41e-1b6d-5177-9642-4f8697bc5ba0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation-Scaling Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "562f2805-9f09-5e89-b09c-94c4809435a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459909} {:answer/id #uuid "feaa5d1c-ea0d-51b8-a656-0e78ecb7f2db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feaa5d1c-ea0d-51b8-a656-0e78ecb7f2db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459910} :answer-field/id #uuid "743ed65d-70d0-5027-9c43-b6b316cce648" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b08d56f9-5c6e-5427-8ac8-973f2cb2c0d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459911} {:answer/id #uuid "f842c9c8-bda5-5681-b9c2-ac48835e9445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b08d56f9-5c6e-5427-8ac8-973f2cb2c0d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459911} :answer-field/id #uuid "21401d46-cadc-5ebc-9505-4a1961e95c21" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "535db015-38fb-51e0-b841-97ef9b67c6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459913} {:answer/id #uuid "bac13582-2752-58d1-a164-33571b4f5329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bac13582-2752-58d1-a164-33571b4f5329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459914} :answer-field/id #uuid "681d3363-4bb9-5097-bd6c-7727036faa45" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3837446-5faf-5668-beb3-7a2ca40df6bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-38517" :question/problem "Which of the following are rotation-scaling matrices?\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- **III.** $C=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A rotation-scaling matrix has the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -b \\\\ b & a\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers that are not equal to zero simultaneously. Notice that the entries on the main diagonal are the same, while the antidiagonal entries have opposite signs.\n\nWith that in mind let's check each of the given matrices:\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ is a rotation-scaling matrix.\n\n- $B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ is *not* a rotation-scaling matrix since the entries on the antidiagonal do not have opposite signs.\n\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ is a rotation-scaling matrix.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129148 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34aa8f4e-20f1-5dda-ac53-6eb411543897" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebe3aa89-50b5-5440-b422-36d3f9494ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459927} {:answer/id #uuid "77bdf90f-936c-580b-899e-22e46c0d53e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebe3aa89-50b5-5440-b422-36d3f9494ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459927} :answer-field/id #uuid "3046a163-3bcd-5cb9-a94b-08ebd4453395" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "508e53ae-e134-512f-b27b-b96ca4e480a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459929} {:answer/id #uuid "741e2816-ff2d-5883-bb18-3878c76ebfbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "508e53ae-e134-512f-b27b-b96ca4e480a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459929} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad65cebe-cec5-5397-8222-8afa8191fa31" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460831} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dc3bca8-7a14-57a9-af87-1a8aaf0f5a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459931} {:answer/id #uuid "49aea637-2b1d-526e-9450-5878abfa1b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49aea637-2b1d-526e-9450-5878abfa1b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459932} :answer-field/id #uuid "74ad5248-f9d9-5ba0-b7d5-e77a1fcce3af" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f40578d-2e88-5fde-bb73-48381fd621fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-38617" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb4959f437e11b767be136a2a024260d45ed29805cd57b1832d74d7cc2da11c1.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n\nII. The degree of $P(x)$ is odd.\n\nIII. The coefficient of the leading term is negative.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6ac301d-037b-5334-b6d2-fec88197d154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459951} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1e6f74-c495-5ab5-805c-d983bca1e55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d1e6f74-c495-5ab5-805c-d983bca1e55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer