6f4-d49a-5e5d-a10c-50a3db34ad1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42006" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "836635cc-25da-5e83-aec4-49f375758900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459957} {:answer/id #uuid "54eea2b5-b542-5880-be19-6f511782168a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "836635cc-25da-5e83-aec4-49f375758900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459957} :answer-field/id #uuid "04197247-7f0f-56bf-a021-b95053e007e5" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29bb0349-8228-5739-b584-2b4184c57825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459959} {:answer/id #uuid "213dd0db-1f16-57b8-a75a-94405f576b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "213dd0db-1f16-57b8-a75a-94405f576b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459960} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1992ae7-8a06-5253-8bae-a159ecd12de1" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460846} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93932082-4e2a-5d11-9338-3badee54015f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459961} {:answer/id #uuid "3337fae3-8c3b-5ced-a2fe-a0e0b650426e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3337fae3-8c3b-5ced-a2fe-a0e0b650426e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459962} :answer-field/id #uuid "da567c2d-7ca3-5ce0-9d1f-676b0894d8d6" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "181e77e0-d595-5539-baef-b4986d4c678b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42024" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bb3ef39-24f4-53fd-ad23-80e8401afa50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460155} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce78283-ea7a-5168-8a04-a0032f00df30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ce78283-ea7a-5168-8a04-a0032f00df30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460156} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5b52c2d-ba98-5b84-9117-102d22385b70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460944} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66729ae8-8043-572c-bc7d-a1c624ce8fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460157} {:answer/id #uuid "9d688561-b6b3-5263-b56a-63b6c54dbfd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d688561-b6b3-5263-b56a-63b6c54dbfd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460158} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7cfdd66-3b1c-5a02-8cb9-f68ca2e8601d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "606315b7-0138-573f-8c5f-15212b7196f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460159} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe69130-7731-5cc0-9c45-c94262ef9b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "606315b7-0138-573f-8c5f-15212b7196f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460159} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9cb025-b523-5afd-9e2b-488c18701756" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de45d0f1-1f5a-51b7-a854-73bfcba5bbdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-71181" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}5x-5, & x<1 \\\\ 0, & x=1 \\\\ {x}^{3}-1, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x)$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=g(1)$\n- **III.** $g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $g(1)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}(5x-5)=5(1)-5=0, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}({x}^{3}-1)={1}^{3}-1=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude that statement I is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=0.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The value of the limit is ${lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=0,$ and the value of the function is $g(1)=0.$ So, statement II is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 1}g(x)=g(1)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, the function is continuous at $x=0,$ and statement III is false.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd96f985-646a-5351-b253-f0f95e8d6cc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460167} {:answer/id #uuid "fec5ba87-c419-560c-b2ba-bfc88d02a82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fec5ba87-c419-560c-b2ba-bfc88d02a82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460168} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ebca1f5-c590-5037-9705-2d669297c270" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a3ff502-9a19-5d3d-b530-9a9bf3e410d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460169} {:answer/id #uuid "45de598b-3b91-5235-928b-a27046c1368a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45de598b-3b91-5235-928b-a27046c1368a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460170} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a62c74-c650-5a78-92c1-6052f0293257" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4406943e-20a0-5c47-9f3b-12422d2366ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460171} {:answer/id #uuid "a14b7932-a9aa-55ab-87a0-b0dcf56024dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4406943e-20a0-5c47-9f3b-12422d2366ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460171} :answer-field/id #uuid "a353e8b3-884f-5bc4-bb00-c6d7f9c98968" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b84b6274-fa65-5873-af84-3d0475556d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-71892" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=1-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=-3?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny=1-{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/72/726ad8599b89029d3dba8e79ca947af99c17bd8712e551e49fc33d3e597a5cb7.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-3\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-y}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-y}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129842 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55a6ee0a-d96f-565a-b86b-753fef10bcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460173} {:answer/id #uuid "c5fa2d01-0363-5414-aee0-15a329ab0bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55a6ee0a-d96f-565a-b86b-753fef10bcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460173} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad56762-b330-5bb1-8ba0-9869f5af2ead" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460953} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f634cf-ea4c-5e68-b5da-4eef1c1c56af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460175} {:answer/id #uuid "49f35556-5b7c-515b-9a7a-4189930ec2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3f634cf-ea4c-5e68-b5da-4eef1c1c56af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460175} :answer-field/id #uuid "409900db-4264-516b-b459-9b27a44721c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ae5851-54cb-53e1-a0fe-3cb10c69a3f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460177} {:answer/id #uuid "58d69edb-8d2a-5ce7-bef1-d0329b4c1d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d69edb-8d2a-5ce7-bef1-d0329b4c1d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460178} :answer-field/id #uuid "f764f310-ac1b-5163-8ef9-b2f704f3384e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7805c1fc-f8dc-58be-9c44-d22a8226c755" :question/math-academy-id "q-71895" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/24/24cbd9a0e01023dca6a289838d94efe3c7b67abe5b7a1f275f6945f280e65d64.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.75$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/6c/6c51abe5c21571a9c5596fce4e3b8ace210eacfab125016e6b9a3b2a7bc2e056.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/f9/f9fed5856eda128d84debec320bc38a35eaa2bf5184b1f81cb1194b02f8a306a.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "503d7110-6cc5-5cf2-87e2-1045c8a36886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459341} {:answer/id #uuid "d57ce771-3028-5baa-b0f2-f4de7d3617d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d57ce771-3028-5baa-b0f2-f4de7d3617d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459342} :answer-field/id #uuid "1af3661f-6783-5478-b5e6-eede91cb4aa6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9564e0ca-db68-5b0e-bdf8-c5593c07408e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459343} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd76439-cdc4-56b2-bd84-3cb9d3bce0cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdd76439-cdc4-56b2-bd84-3cb9d3bce0cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459344} :answer-field/id #uuid "80d76efe-3861-569a-b729-ec393ecd874e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60137c2c-ff15-5a99-a0a7-4cfa1f1442f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459345} {:answer/id #uuid "cff078f1-3b0f-5053-b2a0-745dbd7d061e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60137c2c-ff15-5a99-a0a7-4cfa1f1442f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459345} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec498012-39b0-5787-b344-2b214924c219" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97d43a34-aeb6-5e6a-8281-47dcdcd73020" :question/math-academy-id "q-100128" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t+1,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2t+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(-1)q(-1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(2t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{0}+(2t){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1} \\\\  & =2(0)\\cdot (0+1)+2(-1)\\cdot ((-1)+1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement II is true since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t,2t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(2t){|}_{0}\\cdot (2t+1){|}_{0}+(2t){|}_{-1}\\cdot (2t+1){|}_{-1} \\\\  & =2(0)\\cdot (2(0)+1)+2(-1)\\cdot (2(-1)+1) \\\\  & =2\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed5c8af7-e617-5e8c-be01-45a26eb17d4d" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthonormal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cd9bc41-3629-5ebf-afea-c0113b438161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459939} {:answer/id #uuid "763adf5e-2985-58f3-878f-af1ceb455a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "763adf5e-2985-58f3-878f-af1ceb455a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459940} :answer-field/id #uuid "dde632b0-d6e8-58ec-9cd5-bd0c49f0ee83" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b82eb3-e682-530a-9b57-96c4abd03d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459941} {:answer/id #uuid "f66df056-7344-564f-ae52-b5ac19725d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31b82eb3-e682-530a-9b57-96c4abd03d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459941} :answer-field/id #uuid "042c272c-0cf3-5204-ba83-2a2159804b8f" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460837} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad484f9b-add0-5ea4-9842-82ad3a504d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459943} {:answer/id #uuid "cccd07d0-d98d-5e3d-9912-da890bbff842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cccd07d0-d98d-5e3d-9912-da890bbff842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459944} :answer-field/id #uuid "605e8aa3-faa7-5df1-aa27-1d2229983479" :answer-field/key "W" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89970297-1b2c-5ba8-b18f-ccd95df5c317" :question/math-academy-id "q-39398" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n- **U.** $U={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **V.** $V={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **W.** $W={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0 \\\\ {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}=1 \\\\ {v}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{3}{10}+\\frac{3}{10}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{9}{10}+\\frac{1}{10}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{9}{10}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=4+9+1=14\\ne 1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{12}{25}-\\frac{12}{25}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{9}{25}+\\frac{16}{25}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{16}{25}+\\frac{9}{25}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $W$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b03ea89-5152-5ff4-813a-ca985d60ed5b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c70e775-e2ea-5880-9766-a759863e80f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459945} {:answer/id #uuid "bd18d096-0ce7-5f4c-89c9-2427688240d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd18d096-0ce7-5f4c-89c9-2427688240d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459946} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd285e45-1587-5995-8414-eb1c2ea5950c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5241e690-f33a-54a5-93ed-5931af0130f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459947} {:answer/id #uuid "018ac307-36aa-5934-8c04-ba6821becb4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5241e690-f33a-54a5-93ed-5931af0130f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459947} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa8089e8-1efa-54cb-b513-323981c5c513" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a709466b-e806-5a2b-a8e5-ce3b8a71f657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459949} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f735b1-c60f-50bf-a2f5-a892299f3d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8f735b1-c60f-50bf-a2f5-a892299f3d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459950} :answer-field/id #uuid "1be6f333-0eca-51dc-8a15-10b5dc865754" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2175cca2-c03f-5359-9970-f5c376ea77b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-39630" :question/problem "For the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $u⊥H,\\,$ where $H={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **II.** $u⊥V,\\,$ where $V={[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **III.** $u⊥W,\\,$ where $W={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $H,V$ and $W$ as ${{h}_{1},{h}_{2}},{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ and ${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 3=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥H.$\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-4)+(-1)\\cdot (-2)=-3\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸V.$ Notice that we stopped after finding the first non-orthogonal vector in the set.\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot 8=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d65d5f6-e3b7-5ee9-95cf-58c3e498a702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459975} {:answer/id #uuid "646a048e-f630-5013-95fe-6659b566a35f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "646a048e-f630-5013-95fe-6659b566a35f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459976} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d3f262-127e-5585-b97c-20a126667044" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8460f2bb-e253-5210-9218-4e96e796beae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459977} {:answer/id #uuid "40f38a8d-b50e-505f-9411-5989253d0642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8460f2bb-e253-5210-9218-4e96e796beae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459977} :answer-field/id #uuid "cde9df91-1435-51c4-9805-9c117768203b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d90e2fb7-b1da-50a5-82da-f4e30f796fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459979} {:answer/id #uuid "8df48ba2-f889-595c-9590-a8404cf9b0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8df48ba2-f889-595c-9590-a8404cf9b0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459980} :answer-field/id #uuid "f677a744-3bd0-564b-ade4-affd6abcf2a2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d571c31-8e0e-520c-b34f-482cf5518003" :question/math-academy-id "q-42458" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has a zero column\n- **II.** $A$ has identical columns\n- **III.** $A$ has identical rows\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c05d4f9-eb1b-59a1-ae0b-5d6869bad7c5" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbac9d6d-45d4-5136-bf5b-083c2757b419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460179} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c459cf-e47e-5a6b-9306-a1204647fdc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4c459cf-e47e-5a6b-9306-a1204647fdc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460180} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b856b25-5fd9-5622-a242-7cea8720d0d6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460956} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a637e26-81c3-5744-ad03-798d29b7967e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460181} {:answer/id #uuid "09f35204-c8ab-52a4-bd7d-3608868a9ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a637e26-81c3-5744-ad03-798d29b7967e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460181} :answer-field/id #uuid "b93bf86b-d526-5213-848a-da369e8a84ca" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460957} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a3a351d-1467-5ea7-bd72-80d0b233aa70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460183} {:answer/id #uuid "27e6529b-e064-5869-8608-e8d719d6e58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a3a351d-1467-5ea7-bd72-80d0b233aa70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460183} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb947e93-9b13-5cf0-a1cf-785b08e6926d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ddcaae1f-cad0-5e0d-8af5-aa602e286e49" :question/math-academy-id "q-73574" :question/problem "![](images/a2/a266f4d3ab4254684c91cb422f96b70a4c9973f587b6afb2cd7af5db45e86561.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=1$, $y=0$, $y=2$, $z=0,$ and $z=4-x-y.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,y)\\le z\\le {f}_{2}(x,y)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type I region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,y)=1$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=4-x-y$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,y)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xy$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II and statement III are false. We have\n\n- the *bottom* surface $z={f}_{1}(x,y)=0$, and\n\n- the *top* surface $z={f}_{2}(x,y)=4-x-y.$\n\n![](images/cd/cd218d4c4ef62d63ae2954c0974fb25a95257d9fc322834b0dec4aae3e8e99fc.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222f50fb-1e6d-551e-968f-50c73844d197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460507} {:answer/id #uuid "44a1d641-30a1-5670-a624-6e0d0235945d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44a1d641-30a1-5670-a624-6e0d0235945d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460508} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea3a75a2-870e-5fbf-8b32-79ded3135f76" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461120} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28c286fa-b1fe-5de9-9f3d-391b223d89db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460509} {:answer/id #uuid "883078f4-006a-5c5e-95a5-6b76ce41b72a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "883078f4-006a-5c5e-95a5-6b76ce41b72a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460510} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b55017-3ba1-5628-9f41-22f729dadf78" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95223db9-c430-5634-a8b3-9b3aac9bcfe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460511} {:answer/id #uuid "ae12af06-acfb-53ad-8b5c-db8297ba04cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95223db9-c430-5634-a8b3-9b3aac9bcfe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460511} :answer-field/id #uuid "7391ba90-c816-58f9-9ce4-2f0c7949edd2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5292a809-1b54-5803-b4fb-793edab32841" :question/math-academy-id "q-98522" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-1,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2t-2.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨t,t-1⟩ \\\\  & =(t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t-1){|}_{0}+(t){|}_{1}\\cdot (t-1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =0\\cdot (0-1)+1\\cdot (1-1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t,2t-2⟩ \\\\  & =(t){|}_{0}\\cdot (2t-2){|}_{0}+(t){|}_{1}\\cdot (2t-2){|}_{1} \\\\  & =0\\cdot (2(0)-2)+1\\cdot (2(1)-2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement III is false. Let's check if ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t).$ Computing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-1,2t-2⟩ \\\\  & =(t-1){|}_{0}\\cdot (2t-2){|}_{0}+(t-1){|}_{1}\\cdot (2t-2){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(0-1)\\cdot (2(0)-2)+(1-1)\\cdot (2(1)-2) \\\\  & =2\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product. So, $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}]}
